```latex
\documentclass{article}
\usepackage{pgffor} % Required for the \foreach command

\begin{document}

\begin{enumerate}
  \foreach \x in {3,4,...,46} {
    \item Section \x
  }
\end{enumerate}

\end{document}
```

This will generate a numbered list with sections from 3 to 46, with the section number displayed before each section title. Note that the `pgffor` package is required for the `\foreach` command to work. You can include it in your LaTeX document by adding `\usepackage{pgffor}` at the beginning of your preamble.

